<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Clan Master and Lords</h1>
<p>The <b>Master</b> heads a clan. There is one Master; the Master can appoint 
<b>Lords</b>, who are second in command.
</p><p>Only the Master can:
</p>
<ul><li>appoint a Lord, or hand the clan over to a new Master (<a cmd='#'>Help Cappoint</a>);</li>
<li>depose a Lord (<a cmd='#'>Help Cdepose</a>);</li>
<li>take money out of the treasury and equipment out of the clan's secret storage without being appointed to it (<a cmd='#'>Help Cwithdraw</a>, <a cmd='#'>Help Cunstore</a>).</li></ul>
<p>The Master and the Lords can:
</p>
<ul><li>take in new members, and remove them (<a cmd='#'>Help Caccept</a>, <a cmd='#'>Help Cremove</a>);</li>
<li>set members' ranks, the titles of the ranks, and members' titles (<a cmd='#'>Help Cpromote</a>, <a cmd='#'>Help Csrank</a>, <a cmd='#'>Help Ctitle</a>).</li></ul>
<p>Some of these are open to high ranks as well: caccept from rank 10, 
cpromote from rank 16, ctitle from rank 21, and appointing treasurers and 
quartermasters, or deposing them, from rank 25. A Master can't leave the 
clan before handing it over (see <a cmd='#'>Help Cdefect</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Clan Commands</a>
